		<div class="texto-blog">					
		<p>In this article we will see how to upload our application to the web with <strong>CodeIgniter 4 Deployment</strong> with the use of composer, <strong>CodeIgniter 4 Migrations</strong> and <strong>CodeIgniter 4 Seeds</strong> the example will be done in a <strong>shared hosting</strong>, i will use the domain provider <a class="text-info" href="https://namecheap.pxf.io/rnOVB5" target="_blank">namecheap</a>.</p>

		<h2>CodeIgniter 4 Deployment on shared hosting</h2>

		{{ include('inc/ad_defect.html.twig') }} 	
		
		<p>For this example we will use a subdomain, you need a domain or subdomain to start, then we will create a user to use <strong>ftp</strong> with the program <a class="text-info" href="https://filezilla-project.org/" target="_blank">filezilla</a>.</p>

		<div class="text-center">

		<img class="img-fluid" src="../assets/img/ci4_deploy1.png" alt="ci4_deploy">

		</div>

		<p>We seek our credentials to continue.</p>

		<div class="text-center">

		<img class="img-fluid" src="../assets/img/ci4_deploy2.png" alt="ci4_deploy">

		</div>

		<p>We will connect to our domain or subdomain to continue..</p>

		<div class="text-center">

		<img class="img-fluid" src="../assets/img/ci4_deploy3.png" alt="ci4_deploy">

		</div>

		<p>We place ourselves at the root of our project, and we will begin to upload all the files.</p>

		<div class="text-center">

		<img class="img-fluid" src="../assets/img/ci4_deploy4.png" alt="ci4_deploy">

		</div>

		<p>To be faster and more efficient we will enter through the terminal to make the necessary configurations.</p>

		<div class="text-center">

		<img class="img-fluid" src="../assets/img/ci4_deploy5.png" alt="ci4_deploy">

		</div>

		<p>We will list all the files and folders.</p>

		<code>ls</code>

		<p>We navigate inside our folder.</p>				

		<code>cd ci4tutorial</code>

		<p>We install the vendor folder with <strong>composer</strong>.</p>				

		<code>composer install</code>

		<p>We will show an <strong>error 500</strong>, now it is necessary to make the corresponding configurations.</p>

		<div class="text-center">

		<img class="img-fluid" src="../assets/img/ci4_deploy6.png" alt="ci4_deploy">

		</div>


		<p>We make the settings with the environment variables, if you work with a database you must create it previously.</p>

		<code>nano .env</code>

		<pre class="text-code">
		<code>
		#--------------------------------------------------------------------
		# ENVIRONMENT
		#--------------------------------------------------------------------
		 CI_ENVIRONMENT = production

		#--------------------------------------------------------------------
		# APP
		#--------------------------------------------------------------------

		 app.baseURL = 'youDomainName'


		#--------------------------------------------------------------------
		# DATABASE
		#--------------------------------------------------------------------

		 database.default.hostname = localhost
		 database.default.database = youDatabase
		 database.default.username = youUsername
		 database.default.password = youPassword
		 database.default.DBDriver = MySQLi
		 database.default.DBPrefix =
		</code>
		</pre>

		<p>Once the connection to the database is established, we will continue with migrations and seeds to work with test data.</p>

		<p>We run all migrations.</p>

		<code>php spark migrate</code>

		<p>We run a seed for the test data with users.</p>

		<code>php spark db:seed UserSeeder</code>		

		<div class="text-center">

		<img class="img-fluid" src="../assets/img/ci4_deploy7.png" alt="ci4_deploy">

		</div>

		<p>Finally we will clear the cache.</p>

		<code>php spark cache:clear</code>				

		</div>

